      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of these numbers. We can do this by finding the prime factorization of each number and then taking the highest power of each prime factor that appears in any of the factorizations.\n\nThe prime factorization of the numbers from 1 to 9 is:\n\n1: 1\n2: 2\n3: 3\n4: 2^2\n5: 5\n6: 2 * 3\n7: 7\n8: 2^3\n9: 3^2\n\nNow, we take the highest power of each prime factor:\n\n2^3 (from 8)\n3^2 (from 9)\n5 (from 5)\n7 (from 7)\n\nFinally, we multiply these highest powers together to find the LCM:\n\nLCM = 2^3 * 3^2 * 5 * 7 = 8 * 9 * 5 * 7 = 2520\n\nTherefore, the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9 is \\boxed{2520}.",
