    "text": "To find the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of these numbers. The LCM of a set of numbers is the smallest number that is divisible by all of them.\n\nWe can find the LCM by prime factorizing each number and then taking the highest power of each prime factor that appears in any of the factorizations.\n\nPrime factorization of the numbers 1 through 9:\n1: 1\n2: 2\n3: 3\n4: 2^2\n5: 5\n6: 2 * 3\n7: 7\n8: 2^3\n9: 3^2\n\nNow, we take the highest power of each prime factor that appears in any of the factorizations:\n2^3 (from 8)\n3^2 (from 6 and 9)\n5 (from 5)\n7 (from 7)\n\nThe LCM is the product of these highest powers:\nLCM = 2^3 * 3^2 * 5 * 7 = 8 * 9 * 5 * 7 = 2520\n\nTherefore, the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9 is 2520.",
